{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790345293,"nonce":"u6j+1IimKUmC5wxuUoUeZqoljUI=","title":"Lua: \u003cconst\u003e folding covers only literals and + - * of number literals","message":"scope.rs is_constant folds a \u003cconst\u003e local only when its value is a literal, a folded const name, or unary minus and + - * over number literals. The reference folds any arithmetic and bitwise operation over numeric constants, folded const names included, and refuses a fold whose float result is 0 or NaN or whose integer division or modulo is by zero.\n\nReproducer:\n\n    local N \u003cconst\u003e = 10\n    local M \u003cconst\u003e = N * 2 + 1\n    local function f() return M end\n    print(debug.getupvalue(f, 1))\n\nlua5.4 prints nothing (M is folded, f has no upvalues); zylua prints M 21. The numbering of every later upvalue of f shifts with it, and a string.dump of f carries M as an upvalue, so the loaded copy returns nil (lua5.4 returns 21).\n\nFound while building string.dump (LO-string-dump).","files":null}]}